    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working correctly. Both files are now created as expected:\n\n\u2705 **FRAI-SPEC.md** - The specification template\n\u2705 **.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml** - The GitHub Actions workflow\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in the `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-754). The handler was only passing the positional arguments to the frai-gate CLI, but not the parsed options like `--ci`.\n\n**The fix:** Changed the approach to use `process.argv` directly to extract all command-line arguments after the 'gate' keyword, preserving both positional arguments and flags. This passes the full argument list to frai-gate, which has its own argument parsing logic.\n\n**Changes made:**\n- Modified the action handler to use `process.argv.indexOf('gate')` and slice everything after it\n- Simplified the code by removing the unnecessary Command parameter\n- Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\nThe `--ci` flag now correctly propagates through the frai CLI to frai-gate, and the GitHub Actions workflow file is created as expected.",
